      "side": 1,
      "message": "I wonder about the \u0027static\u0027.\n\nThat mean that if BT does ON -\u003e BLE_ON -\u003e ON, the sEventLogger will not be reset.\nI would recommand to do either:\n* not a static, to only keep current information of LeAudio\n* log in the constructor and in the cleanup method, to make it obvious in the eventLogger when this service got all the field re-initialized\n\nI have a preference for the first one, as re-using same logger between multiples Bluetooth lifecycle can be very confusing and is not guaranteed to always work as LeAudio has no control over BLuetooth going BLE_ON or OFF",
      "revId": "2e96df5cb6350a0df0c9072794a43ab2d0f83929",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
